From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:17:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] runtime: apply fastcopy to gfx125 waitsignal path

Route the gfx125-plus fused WaitSignal SDMA path through the same generic host-accessible fast-copy eligibility helper used by ordinary linear copies. Dependency, profiling, D2D, invalid-range and other ineligible cases continue through the existing path. The current gfx950 target cannot execute this branch, so acceptance is limited to source review and a focused ROCr build; no gfx125 runtime claim is made.

Checkpoint-ID: CP-0056
Goal-ID: GSIM-001
Plan-Revision: 16
Source-Lock-SHA256: 8c0a6d1d04d5a73ab036ddc56d09ff59f7513077931868bdfac5a763f85a73d4
Evidence-Manifest-SHA256: 04ca73c2f7a9c68c5fbba028b3c72021fc9248825dfe410168be255764fb5cd4
Change-Kind: bugfix
Baseline-Commit: cc2d5989ca03307dceb2bf473e5f95ea05fa0236
---
 .../hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_gpu_agent.cpp     | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_gpu_agent.cpp b/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_gpu_agent.cpp
index 7bbfba9b46..b9de23e333 100644
--- a/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_gpu_agent.cpp
+++ b/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_gpu_agent.cpp
@@ -1473,6 +1473,20 @@ hsa_status_t GpuAgent::DmaCopyOnEngine(void* dst, core::Agent& dst_agent,
   if (blit->isSDMA()) {
     BlitSdmaBase* sdma_blit = static_cast<BlitSdmaBase*>((*blit).get());
     if (sdma_blit->IsGfx125Plus()) {
+      // This fused path bypasses the regular SubmitLinearCopyCommand entry
+      // point, where all other blits run the same eligibility check.
+      std::vector<core::Signal*> no_gang;
+      const auto fast_copy = TryHostAccessibleFastCopy(
+          dst, src, size, &dep_signals, &out_signal, &no_gang);
+      if (fast_copy == FastCopyResult::Success) {
+        LogPrint(HSA_AMD_LOG_FLAG_BLIT_KERNEL_PKTS,
+                 "[ROCDTIF SDMA WaitSignal] Fast copy success: src=%p, dst=%p, size=0x%lx",
+                 src, dst, size);
+        return HSA_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+      }
+      if (fast_copy == FastCopyResult::InvalidArgument) {
+        return HSA_STATUS_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT;
+      }
       return sdma_blit->SubmitLinearCopyBodyWaitSignal(
           dst, src, size, dep_signals, out_signal);
     }
